The molecule 3D Transformer is employed to extract the three-dimensional structural information features of molecules. These three-dimensional structural details include the atomic type sequences, atomic three-dimensional coordinates, Euclidean distance matrices between atoms, and matrices representing the types of bonds between atoms in ionizable lipid molecules. TransLNP adopts a pre-training followed by fine-tuning training approach shown in Fig. 2A. Despite the scarcity of labeled data with LNPs properties in the LNPs field, we can leverage various molecular structure information from other small molecules to train the model. The pre-training task utilizes masked language modeling: randomly masking 15\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
