$10^{1.69}$\end{document} times higher than the other. The two molecules differ by only one carbon atom (C) and one nitrogen atom (N) in structure. The attention scores corresponding to the differing C and N atoms are 0.84 and 0.86, significantly higher than the attention scores for other atoms. Therefore, TransMA can identify the key atoms affecting transfection efficiency, demonstrating the interpretability of the model.

